WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.210
(host)
Humans have
domesticated animals

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:04.462
as beasts of burden
for thousands of years.

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:06.131
And the vital role horses play

00:00:06.214 --> 00:00:08.842
in the evolution of
culture in particular

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.720
has inspired countless
equine folklore.

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:14.556
But none are quite
like the centaur.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.559
With the lower body of a horse
and upper body of a human,

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.144
they maybe should be dismissed

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.521
as a completely
impractical creature.

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.314
But even with dubious origins,

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:26.317
history has embraced
the lore of the centaur.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:32.240
I'm Dr. Emily Zarka,
and this is "Monstrum."

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:34.659
A centaur is always
upper half human

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:38.121
and mostly always
lower half male horse.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.332
The centaurs of antiquity
were not known to be docile,

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:42.792
quite the opposite.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.837
They were violent meat
eating predatory creatures

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.548
that hunted and
terrorized humans.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.675
In lore, the human
half of the centaur

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.469
often represents civility,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.429
while the horse
half is bestiality

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:56.347
and uncontrollable desire.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:58.641
Depictions of centaurs
trace the monster back

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.854
as far as the Babylonian
period in the 16th century BCE,

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.939
to when the Kassites
entered the Fertile Crescent

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:08.943
on horseback and seized control
of Southern Mesopotamia.

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:11.696
They used carved boundary
stones called kudurru

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.822
to indicate land transactions.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.992
Some of these artifacts
depict centaurs,

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.370
a human man attached at
the torso to the body and legs

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:20.705
of a winged horse.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:25.001
In examples produced
between 1186 to 1172 BCE

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.878
near what is now Iraq,

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:30.215
the centaurs are depicted
hunting with bows and weapons

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:34.135
and likely served as symbols
of protection or warning.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.012
Kassite influence
likely extended

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:39.641
to the Aegean civilizations,
including the Mycenaean Greeks.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:42.977
While it is unknown exactly
when their cultures interacted,

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:46.481
many scholars believe that
the two influenced one another

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:49.025
and they may have introduced
the idea of the centaur

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.946
to Greece where it really took
hold in folklore and culture.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:55.073
The centaur began to
appear in Greek art

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:57.700
beginning in the
10th century BCE.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.619
The Lefkandi Centaur
is believed to be

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:01.329
the oldest such example.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:04.541
While all four legs of the
centaur appear to be hooved,

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.334
bronze and terracotta artifacts

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.670
from sixth and
eighth century BCE

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:12.298
show the centaur with the
full legged body of a man

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:13.633
with the rear end of a horse

00:02:13.716 --> 00:02:15.677
seemingly grafted onto the back.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.554
Around the eighth century BCE,

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.348
two centaur origin stories
dominate Greek texts,

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:22.350
the benevolent demigod Chiron,

00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:27.063
the immortal instructor, and
the vicious race of Centaurs.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.399
Chiron is the half-horse,
half-human son

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:34.070
of a nymph named Philyra and
the Greek god of time, Kronos.

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.282
Versions differ on who exactly
is genetically responsible

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:38.867
for Chiron's horse half.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.661
In some versions, Philyra
desperately shape shifts

00:02:41.744 --> 00:02:45.039
into a mare to avoid
Kronos' unwanted advances,

00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:47.292
only to have him take
the form of a stallion

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.793
and attack her anyway.

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:50.169
In the other version,

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:52.505
the two are happily
engaged in an affair

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:55.842
until they are caught in the
act by Kronos' wife Rhea.

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:57.135
To avoid being caught,

00:02:57.218 --> 00:02:59.679
the god of time quickly
shifted into a horse

00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:02.223
to avoid his wife
identifying him.

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:05.685
Philyra is horrified when
she births a half horse baby

00:03:05.768 --> 00:03:07.353
and abandons him.

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.522
Apollo and Artemis
take the child in

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:11.691
and under their
divine instruction,

00:03:11.774 --> 00:03:14.527
the Chimera demigod
becomes a notable healer,

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:16.863
astrologer, hunter, and prophet.

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:19.532
He marries a nymph and they
have multiple children.

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:23.202
He also becomes a teacher
to infamous heroes Perseus,

00:03:23.286 --> 00:03:24.662
Achilles and Heracles.

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:28.041
In the early fifth century,
ancient Greek poet Pindar

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:31.669
gives us the second canonical
centaur origin story,

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:33.880
that of Ixion and
the race of Centaurs

00:03:33.963 --> 00:03:35.006
who are far less noble.

00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:38.509
These creatures are the
grandchildren of Ixion,

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.595
king of the Lapiths and Nephele,

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:43.431
who's basically a cloud
made into a beautiful woman.

00:03:43.514 --> 00:03:45.516
After Ixion assaults Nephele,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.894
she gives birth to a unique son.

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:49.520
Depending on the story,

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:52.190
this is either
the first horse-human hybrid,

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:53.900
a true monster,

00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:56.903
or a human man named Centaurus

00:03:56.986 --> 00:04:00.448
who would eventually mate
with multiple Magnesian mares,

00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:03.952
unions that all resulted in
herds of hybrid children.

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:06.204
Either way, it's a dark story.

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:08.289
The race of Centaurs
are often portrayed

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:11.084
as lust-filled drunk,
dangerous beings.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.669
Sexual assault and violence

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.296
underscore almost
all encounters.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:18.466
And that's before we get
into the Centauromachy,

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.760
or what I like to call
the bloody wedding.

00:04:20.843 --> 00:04:23.638
The Centauromachy is a key
part of Greek mythology,

00:04:23.721 --> 00:04:26.599
an epic battle between the
Centaurs and the Lapiths,

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:29.686
an Aeolian tribe, that
began when the hybrid race

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.563
got really drunk and tried
to rape all the women

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:34.649
at the wedding,
including the bride.

00:04:34.732 --> 00:04:37.485
For the Greeks, the Centaur
race was a representation

00:04:37.568 --> 00:04:39.529
of dangerous hyper-masculinity.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.780
They can't hold their liquor

00:04:40.863 --> 00:04:43.282
and they're physically
and sexually violent.

00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:45.201
Homer refers to the
race of Centaurs

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.203
as mountain-bred animals.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.413
For the ancient Greeks,

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:50.707
the mountains were
synonymous with danger,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.042
directly opposing
the groomed fertile plains

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.169
associated with civilization.

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:57.588
The connection between
centaurs and sexuality,

00:04:57.672 --> 00:05:00.508
particularly sex outside
of a marital union,

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:02.218
marks them as ready metaphors

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:04.971
condemning such practices
in the real world,

00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:08.683
given that they are
also associated with
negative animality.

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:11.060
Just look at the Centaurs'
forefather Ixion.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:14.105
He gets out of paying a dowry
by killing his father-in-law,

00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:16.733
tries to seduce Zeus'
sister slash wife

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.151
and gets with a cloud,

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.820
not exactly a pillar
of the community.

00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:24.282
And he ends up pinned to a
flaming wheel for all eternity.

00:05:24.365 --> 00:05:26.200
The entire history
of the centaurs

00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:29.412
from their very creation
is marked with negativity.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.830
According to Greek lore,

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.999
all the centaurs were
slaughtered by Heracles

00:05:33.082 --> 00:05:36.794
after a centaur named Nessus
tried to steal Heracles' bride.

00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:38.504
Chiron tries to intervene,

00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:40.548
but is grazed by
a poisoned arrow.

00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:42.675
Unable to die but in great pain,

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:46.679
he exchanges his immortality
for Prometheus's freedom.

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.848
Upon his death, he is
placed in the stars

00:05:48.931 --> 00:05:53.102
as the constellation
Centaurus or Sagittarius.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:56.314
Chiron is the only exception
to centaurs' representation

00:05:56.397 --> 00:05:58.816
of the supposedly
uncivilized other.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.818
And the Greek's attempts
to demonize cultures

00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:02.320
they found barbaric.

00:06:02.403 --> 00:06:04.655
Unpredictable, on the
fringes of society,

00:06:04.739 --> 00:06:08.367
and more animal than human,
they provide a ready scapegoat,

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:11.788
one that unfortunately would
be applied to real people.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.457
Ancient Greek and Roman art
suggests that the centaurs

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.043
were metaphorical
exaggerated representations

00:06:17.126 --> 00:06:19.045
of the Persians,
replacing real outsiders

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:22.548
with monstrous,
fictional outsiders.

00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:24.509
It has also been argued
that the Centauromachy

00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:26.344
may be a fictional
representation

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:28.054
of the real conflict

00:06:28.137 --> 00:06:31.641
between the Argive and Theban
people before 1200 BCE.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.267
Hailing from the Argos region,

00:06:33.351 --> 00:06:36.562
the Argives were famous for
their horses and agriculture.

00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:38.314
The aptly named city of Thebes

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:41.150
was an influential hub of trade.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.653
The Parthenon in Greece
includes the Centauromachy

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.113
and its architecture.

00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.448
The marble sculptures
depicting the monsters

00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:50.409
as muscular threatening
opponents to the humans

00:06:50.493 --> 00:06:52.912
rearing triumphantly
over their kills.

00:06:52.995 --> 00:06:54.997
The temple of Apollo Epikourios

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.626
is also adorned with images
from the Centauromachy,

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:01.587
but the centaur's human
heads are older bearded men

00:07:01.671 --> 00:07:04.048
and the assaults are
more sexually graphic.

00:07:04.132 --> 00:07:06.801
In all these hard won
centaur human battles,

00:07:06.884 --> 00:07:09.095
the Greek male
citizen triumphed,

00:07:09.178 --> 00:07:10.555
emphasizing their importance

00:07:10.638 --> 00:07:11.889
and visibility in Greek culture.

00:07:11.973 --> 00:07:15.101
During and after the
real Persian Wars,

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:17.603
the creation of the
city-state or polis

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:18.855
bound Greeks together

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:21.065
with a centralized
democratic government

00:07:21.149 --> 00:07:21.899
and a shared language.

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:24.527
Social hierarchy
within the polis

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.612
was determined by
birth and gender.

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:29.907
At the top, free adult
men born legitimately

00:07:29.991 --> 00:07:33.744
to citizen parents, aka the
heroes of the Centaur stories.

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:36.539
Below them, foreigners
and foreign residents,

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.541
aka the centaurs.

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:41.210
In an effort to establish
legitimate citizenship

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:45.131
for Greek heirs, Greek men were
to marry virgin Greek women.

00:07:45.214 --> 00:07:47.383
Foreigners, depicted
as centaurs,

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.510
threatened Greek
citizenship and government

00:07:49.594 --> 00:07:51.762
with their sexual
lasciviousness.

00:07:51.846 --> 00:07:53.306
There is some
argument to be made

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:55.766
about the novelty of
the rider on horseback

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:58.394
when such mounts were first
encountered by cultures

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:02.023
whose ecosystems did not
naturally include horses.

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:05.651
Whether seen first in
war, trade or conquest,

00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.945
the shock of seeing
a human on horseback

00:08:08.029 --> 00:08:11.490
may have given some
inspiration for the centaur.

00:08:11.574 --> 00:08:14.410
To that point, some scholars
argue that the centaur myth

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:16.621
may be based on the
first mountain riders

00:08:16.704 --> 00:08:18.206
in the Thessaly region,

00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:20.625
pre-Trojan war tribes
believed to be named

00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:22.668
Centaur and Lapith.

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:26.130
The Centaur people according
to Greek author Palaephatus

00:08:26.214 --> 00:08:28.633
hailed from a village
named Nephele.

00:08:28.716 --> 00:08:30.468
During Ixion's reign as king,

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:33.179
a herd of wild bulls
terrorized the region

00:08:33.262 --> 00:08:36.307
and inhabitants of Nephele were
the only ones daring enough

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.601
to ride horses into
the herd of bulls,

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.019
slaying them with javelins.

00:08:40.102 --> 00:08:42.855
After they were
rewarded by the king,

00:08:42.939 --> 00:08:45.983
they turned hostile toward
the townspeople of Larissa,

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:49.195
called Lapiths, kidnapping
women and burning homes

00:08:49.278 --> 00:08:51.447
before retreating
to the mountains.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.617
But Palaephatus is known for
trying to rationalize myths,

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.744
so who really knows?

00:08:56.827 --> 00:08:58.788
Other attempts to bring
the centaur to reality

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:02.166
include pre-Socratic Greek
philosopher Empedocles,

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.627
who proposed a theory
of human evolution

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.836
that included the centaurs

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.631
as part of ancient
generations of animals

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.676
that existed before
species differentiation.

00:09:11.759 --> 00:09:14.887
There were also reports
of real centaurs.

00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:15.930
In the early first century CE,

00:09:16.013 --> 00:09:18.975
Roman Emperor
Claudius received word

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:21.227
that a centaur had been found.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.937
Reportedly captured in Arabia

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.064
and transported to Egypt
as a gift for the emperor,

00:09:25.147 --> 00:09:27.858
it was said that the
meat eating creature

00:09:27.942 --> 00:09:30.152
did not survive the
change in climate.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:33.781
After its death, it was
embalmed and sent to Rome.

00:09:33.864 --> 00:09:36.158
Emperor Claudius displayed
the embalmed centaur

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.744
with a face fiercer
than a human face,

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:42.540
hairy arms and hands
and a tawny mane at his palace.

00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:44.375
While this story
seems like fiction,

00:09:44.458 --> 00:09:47.837
there is a bit of fact,
or rather trickery.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.880
The supposed centaur
submerged in honey

00:09:49.964 --> 00:09:52.216
was likely made from
the mummified remains

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.176
of humans and horses.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.178
The honey not only
preserved the corpse

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:58.389
but would've been
difficult to look through.

00:09:58.472 --> 00:10:01.434
A blurry centaur is
more easily believed.

00:10:01.517 --> 00:10:05.021
The creature was still on
view nearly a century later.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:06.689
You would think such hoaxes

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:09.567
would've faded with
the development of
biological studies.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:12.653
But in the 1980s,
a supposed centaur skeleton

00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:14.530
was exhibited in the US.

00:10:14.613 --> 00:10:18.075
Created by zoologist William
Willers as a social experiment,

00:10:18.159 --> 00:10:21.162
the remains now reside in
the John C. Hodges Library

00:10:21.245 --> 00:10:23.414
at the University of
Tennessee-Knoxville

00:10:23.497 --> 00:10:25.124
as an art installation.

00:10:25.207 --> 00:10:27.168
Beginning in the
sixth century CE,

00:10:27.251 --> 00:10:30.421
centaurs and satyrs became
increasingly conflated,

00:10:30.504 --> 00:10:33.591
with the former disappearing
from the retelling of myths

00:10:33.674 --> 00:10:35.760
even though their
image remained in art.

00:10:35.843 --> 00:10:38.346
It seems the centaurs
were too supernatural,

00:10:38.429 --> 00:10:39.722
too uncivilized.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:41.390
However, in the Middle Ages,

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:44.852
centaurs began reappearing
in Christian churches.

00:10:44.935 --> 00:10:46.896
Associated with bestial desires

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:49.231
or even the devil on
the hunt for souls,

00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:52.318
they retained the negative
associations of the past.

00:10:52.401 --> 00:10:55.696
Centaurs would go on to appear
in Dante's "Divine Comedy"

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.698
as the inhabitants
of the first ring

00:10:57.782 --> 00:10:59.158
of the seventh circle of hell.

00:10:59.241 --> 00:11:01.535
You know, the one with
the river of blood.

00:11:01.619 --> 00:11:03.954
They stand on the banks
as jailers of the souls

00:11:04.038 --> 00:11:05.539
boiling in the river,

00:11:05.623 --> 00:11:08.084
shooting arrows at
any who try to escape.

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:11.921
Centaurs increasingly moved
from presumed fact to fiction.

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.089
By the 19th century,

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:14.840
interpretations of the centaur

00:11:14.924 --> 00:11:16.175
focused on their
connection to nature,

00:11:16.258 --> 00:11:19.303
with the creatures
personifying tornadoes

00:11:19.387 --> 00:11:20.930
or mountain streams.

00:11:21.013 --> 00:11:23.224
Centaurs today occupy
the fantasy genre,

00:11:23.307 --> 00:11:24.892
appearing in books and movies

00:11:24.975 --> 00:11:27.770
as dangerous but
fantastic creatures.

00:11:27.853 --> 00:11:29.522
Given the genre's mass appeal

00:11:29.605 --> 00:11:31.649
and often younger
target demographic,

00:11:31.732 --> 00:11:34.485
the brutal violence,
particularly sexual violence,

00:11:34.568 --> 00:11:36.654
is mostly downplayed in favor

00:11:36.737 --> 00:11:38.572
of more culturally
digestible pieces

00:11:38.656 --> 00:11:39.865
of the monster's
ancient origins.

00:11:39.949 --> 00:11:42.493
In C.S. Lewis's
"Chronicles of Narnia,"

00:11:42.576 --> 00:11:45.329
they are strong,
noble, bearded warriors

00:11:45.413 --> 00:11:47.498
who fight for good along Aslan.

00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:48.791
While physically imposing,

00:11:48.874 --> 00:11:50.751
Lewis makes sure
centaur characters

00:11:50.835 --> 00:11:53.754
are positioned as
educated civilized allies,

00:11:53.838 --> 00:11:56.674
who excel in medicine
and reading the stars.

00:11:56.757 --> 00:11:58.634
In J.K. Rowling's
Harry Potter series,

00:11:58.717 --> 00:12:00.970
centaurs are likewise
intelligent healers

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:04.598
and quite skilled at archery,
astronomy, and divination.

00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:07.101
Almost all choose to
remain apart from humans,

00:12:07.184 --> 00:12:08.894
seeing them as
unworthy of attention

00:12:08.978 --> 00:12:12.064
since they have already read
their fates in the stars.

00:12:12.148 --> 00:12:13.732
Even though Rowling's
interpretation

00:12:13.816 --> 00:12:15.776
attempts to make the
creatures respectable,

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.737
they are also portrayed
as wild and uncivilized

00:12:18.821 --> 00:12:20.322
which takes a disturbing turn

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:23.701
when temporary Hogwarts
Headmistress Dolores Umbridge

00:12:23.784 --> 00:12:25.953
is carried off by
centaurs into the woods

00:12:26.036 --> 00:12:28.497
and returns
incapable of speaking

00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:31.709
with bits of twigs and leaves
and her disheveled hair.

00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:34.712
Rowling's centaurs seem
to retain as much of Ixion

00:12:34.795 --> 00:12:35.963
as they do of Chiron.

00:12:36.046 --> 00:12:39.675
I'm sorry Professor,
I must not tell lies.

00:12:39.758 --> 00:12:41.260
What are you doing?!

00:12:41.343 --> 00:12:44.096
(Dr. Zarka)
In Rick Riordan's
"Percy Jackson" series,

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.098
the original Chiron
of Greek myth

00:12:46.182 --> 00:12:48.100
teaches the heroes of the story,

00:12:48.184 --> 00:12:49.977
at first choosing to
hide the lower half

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.395
of his body with a blanket

00:12:51.479 --> 00:12:53.814
and a wheeled box
with fake human legs.

00:12:53.898 --> 00:12:55.149
In the books at least.

00:12:55.232 --> 00:12:57.067
The Centaur race also appears,

00:12:57.151 --> 00:13:01.030
described as talented
warriors and big partiers.

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:03.365
While threads of the
original centaurs linger,

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.743
today the centaur is
more commonly used

00:13:05.826 --> 00:13:07.745
as a symbol that unites

00:13:07.828 --> 00:13:10.122
rather than divides
humans and animals.

00:13:10.206 --> 00:13:12.124
Because the centaur is
made from two beings

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:15.377
that really exist, not
entirely fictional beasts,

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:17.296
they are more
easily transmissible

00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:19.381
and translatable across time.

00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:20.841
Positive or negative,

00:13:20.925 --> 00:13:22.801
they force us to
confront our relationship

00:13:22.885 --> 00:13:25.804
with non-human animals
as both celebration

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:29.600
and condemnation of the
human animal relationship.

00:13:29.683 --> 00:13:32.019
Wes, a bro--
a bronze arrowhead.

00:13:33.938 --> 00:13:36.524
The brutal violence,
particularly sexual violence,

00:13:36.607 --> 00:13:38.275
is mostly down paid-

00:13:39.527 --> 00:13:42.488
Epikori--
It's definitely Epikourios.

00:13:42.571 --> 00:13:43.697
Epikourios.

00:13:43.781 --> 00:13:46.075
At first choosing to hide.

